This PR removes `locale: true` from the module-level `userSelect` in `UserRepository`:

::diff{file="packages/features/users/repositories/UserRepository.ts" lines="96-104"}

The cancellation flow now loads the organizer through `userRepository.findByIdOrThrow`, which calls `findById`, which selects `userSelect`. As a result, `organizer.locale` is always `undefined`, so these lines always fall back to English:

::code{file="packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts" lines="337-337"}

::code{file="packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts" lines="370-370"}

::callout{type="warning"}
`userSelect` is also used at lines 177, 205, 275, 379 and 432 of `UserRepository.ts`. Every caller of those methods silently loses `locale` too. The return type also no longer contains `locale`, which can break type-checking for consumers that read it.

The old inline Prisma query selected `locale` explicitly. Put it back:

::suggestion{file="packages/features/users/repositories/UserRepository.ts" lines="100-101"}
  completedOnboarding: true,
  locale: true,
  timeFormat: true,

For "cancel all remaining", `updateMany` still filters with `gte = new Date()`. The follow-up `findMany` now filters with `gte: bookingToDelete.startTime`. Before, it used `new Date()`:

::diff{file="packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts" lines="497-521"}

When `allRemainingBookings` is set and `cancelSubsequentBookings` isn't, the two queries cover different ranges:
- **`bookingToDelete` is in the past:** `findMany` returns past occurrences that were **not** cancelled. Those get deleted workflow reminders (including after-event reminders), deleted scheduled webhook triggers and no-show tasks, and `onBulkBookingsCancelled` audit events claiming they were cancelled.
- **`bookingToDelete` is a future occurrence:** occurrences between now and its start time are cancelled by `updateMany` but skipped by `findMany`. Their reminders and webhook triggers stay alive, and they get no audit entry.

The PR describes itself as a no-behavior-change refactor. Use the same `gte` for both queries:

::suggestion{file="packages/features/bookings/lib/handleCancelBooking.ts" lines="513-520"}
    const allUpdatedBookings = await bookingRepository.findManyIncludeWorkflowRemindersAndReferences({
      where: {
        recurringEventId: bookingToDelete.recurringEventId,
        startTime: {
          gte,
        },
      },
    });

Three new DI modules import `moduleLoader` from `@calcom/prisma/prisma.module`, but `packages/prisma` has no such file. The existing loader lives at `@calcom/features/di/modules/Prisma`, which is what `BookingCancelService.module.ts` used before this PR.

::diff{file="packages/features/bookings/di/BookingReferenceRepository.module.ts" lines="1-4"}

`BookingReferenceRepository.module.ts` also imports `BookingReferenceRepository` from `@calcom/lib/server/repository/bookingReference`. That path doesn't exist either: the class lives in `@calcom/features/bookingReference/repositories/BookingReferenceRepository`.

The same Prisma import appears in ::file{file="packages/features/bookings/di/BookingAttendeeRepository.module.ts"} and ::file{file="packages/features/users/di/Profile.module.ts"}.

`BookingCancelService.module.ts` imports all three modules. Type-checking will fail, and `getBookingCancelService()` will throw a module-resolution error as soon as anything uses it. Today its only call site, in `apps/web/app/api/cancel/route.ts`, is commented out, which is probably why nothing caught this.

::suggestion{file="packages/features/bookings/di/BookingReferenceRepository.module.ts" lines="3-4"}
import { BookingReferenceRepository } from "@calcom/features/bookingReference/repositories/BookingReferenceRepository";
import { moduleLoader as prismaModuleLoader } from "@calcom/features/di/modules/Prisma";

The interface says `updateMany` returns `Promise<{ count: number }>`:

::code{file="packages/lib/server/repository/dto/IBookingRepository.ts" lines="46-55"}

The implementation `await`s the call and returns nothing, so it returns `Promise<void>`:

::diff{file="packages/features/bookings/repositories/BookingRepository.ts" lines="1502-1507"}

Because the class declares `implements IBookingRepository`, this should be a type error. The interface also leaves out `updateIncludeWorkflowRemindersAndReferences`, which is the method the single-booking path actually calls. Meanwhile `update` is declared but never used in the cancellation flow.

Separately, `handler`'s `Dependencies` type uses the concrete classes (`BookingRepository`, `PrismaBookingAttendeeRepository`) rather than the new interfaces. That undercuts the stated goal of making the flow testable with fakes.
